.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt ISH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ish
.Nd freestanding command shell
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl c Ar COMMAND
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the command shell of the test and os-simple images.
It is a static i386 program with its own startup code and system-call
wrappers and links no C library.
It runs one command at a time.
It is not a POSIX shell and has no script language.
.Pp
In interactive mode,
.Nm
reads standard input until end of file and prints no prompt.
The input buffer holds 255 bytes; the argument array holds 255 tokens.
.Pp
With
.Fl c ,
.Nm
runs one command and exits with its status.
Only
.Ql argv[2]
is used as the command.
.Pp
The parser splits words on ASCII whitespace.
It implements no quotes, escapes, variables, globbing, pipelines,
command lists, subshells, or background jobs.
For external commands, the separate tokens
.Ql <
and
.Ql >
redirect standard input and standard output.
The arguments must come before the redirections, and when both streams
are redirected the output must come before the input; a form that breaks
this order loses the arguments or the output redirection.
Output redirection creates the file with requested mode 0644, subject to
the file-creation mask, or truncates an existing file.
The files are opened for a builtin too, though a builtin's streams are not
redirected.
.Pp
The builtins are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm cd Op Ar DIR
Change the working directory to
.Ar DIR ,
or to
.Ev HOME
when no directory is given.
The status is 0 on success and 1 on failure.
.It Cm exit Op Ar STATUS
Exit the shell with the given status.
.El
.Pp
An external command is tried as written, then through each nonempty element of
.Ev PATH .
A constructed path is limited to 1024 bytes.
The child inherits the shell's environment.
.Pp
On os-simple, the shell is installed as
.Pa /bin/ish
and
.Pa /bin/sh ;
on the test image, as
.Pa /ish
and
.Pa /bin/sh .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
With
.Fl c ,
the status is the child's exit status after a normal exit,
127 when no executable path resolves,
126 when the command cannot be started, or
.Ql 128 + SIGNAL
when a signal kills the child.
Interactive mode discards each command's status.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sh 1 ,
.Xr rach2 7
